# LAST-MINUTE VIVA REVISION

Remember these important differences:

| Question | One-line answer |
|---|---|
| Git vs GitHub | Git tracks versions; GitHub hosts repositories. |
| Git Add vs Commit | Add stages changes; Commit saves changes. |
| Git Push vs Pull | Push uploads; Pull downloads and integrates. |
| Fetch vs Pull | Fetch downloads; Pull downloads and integrates. |
| Merge vs Rebase | Merge combines branches; Rebase moves commits onto another base. |
| CI vs CD | CI automates integration and testing; CD automates delivery or deployment. |
| Docker vs Kubernetes | Docker runs containers; Kubernetes manages containers. |
| Image vs Container | Image is a template; Container is its running instance. |
| VM vs Container | VM has a guest OS; Container shares the host kernel. |
| Git vs SVN | Git is distributed; SVN is centralized. |
| Jenkins vs Docker | Jenkins automates workflows; Docker packages and runs applications. |

